<title>MEXICO: Mexico C/A gap seen at 3.2 pct/GDP by 2000 - gov't.</title>
<headline>Mexico C/A gap seen at 3.2 pct/GDP by 2000 - gov't.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's current account deficit will steadily widen to reach 3.2 percent of gross domestic product by the year 2000, the government said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Outlining its economic plans in the National Program for Financing Development 1997-2000, the government said the current account deficit would be as follows:</p>
<p>    YEAR		AMOUNT</p>
<p>    1995		-7.0 (actual)</p>
<p>    1996		-0.6 (actual)</p>
<p>    1997		-1.6</p>
<p>    1998		-2.2</p>
<p>    1999		-2.6</p>
<p>    2000		-3.2</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
